WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
Read this sentence aloud.

2
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.390
"The list of names are long.

3
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.250
" It sounds fine, doesn't it?

4
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.610
The word names is plural, so
the verb are feels right.

5
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.910
But is the sentence right?

6
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.030
Which word does the verb
really have to agree with?

7
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.250
In this mission, you'll find
out what Standard English is,

8
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.870
and when you need it.

9
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.330
You'll keep your tense
and agreement steady.

10
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.470
You'll build new words from
prefixes, roots and suffixes.

11
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.670
And you'll see how a short
sentence can hit hard.

12
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.990
Your mission: find the subject,

13
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.430
then fix the verb if it needs fixing.
